{"abstract":"Repair of double-strand DNA breaks generated by site-directed endonucleases, like Cas9, is the hallmark of gene editing based on homology-directed repair (HDR). HDR uses an exogenous DNA template to restore the cleaved DNA sequence and can facilitate specific gene corrections as well as insertion of genes or partial complementary DNA (cDNA) sequences. For CRISPR/Cas-directed gene editing, co-administration of the Cas9/single guide RNA (sgRNA) ribonucleoprotein (RNP) complex and a DNA template typically involves two different delivery strategies or different types of vehicles. This requires exquisite timing of delivery and may potentially challenge safety and therapeutic applicability. There is a need therefore for technologies that can ferry complete editing tool kits into cells. Here, we demonstrate the use of lentivirus-derived nanoparticles (LVNPs) to transport both RNP complexes and vector RNA, which upon reverse transcription serves as a repair template for HDR-directed gene editing. Such 'all-in-one' LVNPs support targeted gene insertion with reduced off-target effects relative to nucleofection procedures. We show potent editing in the HBB gene in human erythroid progenitor cells as well as HDR-directed editing in hematopoietic stem and progenitor cells. Our findings mark a first step toward using a single virus-derived vehicle for delivering a full HDR gene editing kit.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Andersen, Sofie","Wolff, Jonas Holst","Skov, Thomas Wisbech","Janns, Jacob Hørlück","Davis, Luther John","Haldrup, Jakob","Haslund, Didde","Revenfeld, Anne Louise Schacht","Relkovic, Dinko","Møller, Bjarne Kuno","Lund, Jacob","Bak, Rasmus O","Thomsen, Emil Aagaard","Mikkelsen, Jacob Giehm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-825921"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gene editing in hematopoietic stem cells by co delivery of cas000000000009 sgrna ribonucleoprotein and templates for homology directed repair in all in one lentivirus derived nanoparticles","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkaf767","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-825921","identifier":[{"id":"PMC12350093","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"40808298","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105013344167","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-9b54bafc-c869-4317-a750-681ff4398a2e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-1435EF6080E2D773348E3FBFFE219ACD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkaf767","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofie","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Sofie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jonas Holst","key":"wolffpau","last":"Wolff","locid":"9b995112-1bc5-4b93-99ae-3b6b707d8571","name":"Wolff, Jonas Holst","orcid":"0000-0001-5690-7603","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Wisbech","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","locid":"2d16933a-9438-4c13-b27a-bd7b1b45469d","name":"Skov, Thomas Wisbech","orcid":"0009-0008-0959-880X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob Hørlück","key":"jannspau","last":"Janns","locid":"30d8584f-59fe-472e-a8ea-69e73cae2656","name":"Janns, Jacob Hørlück","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luther John","key":"davispau","last":"Davis","locid":"a41cd268-707c-4dd1-881b-cced8afd5043","name":"Davis, Luther John","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob H","key":"haldruppau","last":"Haldrup","locid":"38ce8dc0-5ce7-4717-be51-9eec11e6629f","name":"Haldrup, Jakob","name_org":"Haldrup, Jakob H","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Didde","key":"haslundpau","last":"Haslund","locid":"52805595-684c-4db7-b6ca-95e8c09f495f","name":"Haslund, Didde","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Louise","key":"revenfeldpau","last":"Revenfeld","locid":"8bb500e3-790a-4014-9bc9-8fe575fa44c1","name":"Revenfeld, Anne Louise Schacht","name_org":"Revenfeld, Anne Louise","orcid":"0000-0003-1840-0259","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dinko","key":"relkovicpau","last":"Relkovic","name":"Relkovic, Dinko","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bjarne K","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"1efb651c-6d14-4c30-82e6-998dbb496ae0","name":"Møller, Bjarne Kuno","name_org":"Møller, Bjarne K","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","name":"Lund, Jacob","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus O","key":"bakpau","last":"Bak","locid":"40bbfca0-53bc-4709-a0fe-6cba19a6cc6c","name":"Bak, Rasmus O","orcid":"0000-0002-7383-0297","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Emil Aagaard","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"3ac09685-7b89-4211-8cc4-db42bf2c57b0","name":"Thomsen, Emil Aagaard","orcid":"0000-0002-2685-7745","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob Giehm","key":"mikkelsenpau","last":"Mikkelsen","locid":"b6e66050-c539-43e7-bacb-b3f0d27b8932","name":"Mikkelsen, Jacob Giehm","orcid":"0000-0002-1322-3209","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40808298"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkaf767","issn":["03051048","13624962"],"issn_org":["03051048"],"issue":"15","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","paperid":"gkaf767","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Nucleic Acids Research","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105013344167"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9b54bafc-c869-4317-a750-681ff4398a2e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Gene editing in hematopoietic stem cells by co-delivery of Cas9/sgRNA ribonucleoprotein and templates for homology-directed repair in 'all-in-one' lentivirus-derived nanoparticles","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-825921","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Healthcare is rapidly moving into the home to address the challenges of rising costs of hospital care, shortage of healthcare staff, and patient preferences. Hospital in the Home (HITH) is one model addressing these challenges; however, this model poses new challenges to the home, patients, relatives, and healthcare professionals. Derived from a transdisciplinary workshop and subsequent collaboration, four themes relevant and essential for future transdisciplinary research on HITH are proposed, namely, 1) HITH Definitions and their Implications; 2) The Home - Materiality, Atmosphere, and Everyday Life; 3) The Professions - the Home as a Workplace for Healthcare Professionals; and 4) Social Networks - Relatives, Patients, and Responsibilities. We argue that a transdisciplinary research- and practice-informed approach to HITH offers integrated problem-solving and the possibility of asking new and innovative questions and reaching a wider professional audience.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Boelsbjerg, Hanne Bess","Klakk, Emma","Traulsen, Janine Morgall","Bruun, Mette Birkedal","Holst Andersen, Jacob","Bangsgaard Antonsen, Louise","Hald Clemmensen, Marianne","Edwards, Kasper","Kruckow, Sarah","Lavesen, Marie","Laursen, Cæcilie S.","Lee, Nicholas Thomas","Meier, Marie","Verner Rossing, Charlotte","Tonning, Julia Aviaja Lindholt","Winther, Ida Wentzel","Nørgaard, Lotte Stig"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-816978"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Centre for Privacy Studies"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"commentary approaching hospitals in the home from a transdisciplinary perspective","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-816978","ids":["au-f6431fb9-2570-4ab1-b87f-47808668179f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-24FA11F7C318BACA49A93B06BB54F723"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Culture and Society, School of Culture and Society - Department of Anthropology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Centre for Privacy Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Emergency Medical Services"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hanne Bess","key":"boelsbjergpau","last":"Boelsbjerg","locid":"ee7e2b13-79f3-43d2-baff-09edb7540240","name":"Boelsbjerg, Hanne Bess","orcid":"0000-0002-1235-0206","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Emma","key":"klakkpau","last":"Klakk","name":"Klakk, Emma","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Janine Morgall","key":"traulsenpau","last":"Traulsen","name":"Traulsen, Janine Morgall","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Birkedal","key":"bruunpau","last":"Bruun","name":"Bruun, Mette Birkedal","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"holstandersenpau","last":"Holst Andersen","name":"Holst Andersen, Jacob","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"bangsgaardantonsenpau","last":"Bangsgaard Antonsen","name":"Bangsgaard Antonsen, Louise","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne","key":"haldclemmensenpau","last":"Hald Clemmensen","name":"Hald Clemmensen, Marianne","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"edwardspau","last":"Edwards","name":"Edwards, Kasper","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah","key":"kruckowpau","last":"Kruckow","name":"Kruckow, Sarah","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"lavesenpau","last":"Lavesen","name":"Lavesen, Marie","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Cæcilie S.","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","name":"Laursen, Cæcilie S.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicholas Thomas","key":"leepau","last":"Lee","name":"Lee, Nicholas Thomas","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"meierpau","last":"Meier","name":"Meier, Marie","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"vernerrossingpau","last":"Verner Rossing","name":"Verner Rossing, Charlotte","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Julia Aviaja Lindholt","key":"tonningpau","last":"Tonning","name":"Tonning, Julia Aviaja Lindholt","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ida Wentzel","key":"wintherpau","last":"Winther","locid":"779cc69a-5f0d-425b-ad81-9a750dc6d234","name":"Winther, Ida Wentzel","orcid":"0000-0002-6060-2148","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lotte Stig","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","name":"Nørgaard, Lotte Stig","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["22813993","22814612"],"issn_org":["22813993"],"journal":"Academic Journal of Interdisciplinary Studies","publisher":"Richtmann Publishing Ltd","status":"s","title":"Academic Journal of Interdisciplinary Studies"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Submitted"]},"sid":["au-f6431fb9-2570-4ab1-b87f-47808668179f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Commentary: Approaching Hospitals in the Home from a Transdisciplinary Perspective","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-816978","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Aim: Gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM) has been associated with reduced postprandial glucagon-like peptide 1 (GLP-1) responses. As pregnancy induces changes in gallbladder motility and bile acids stimulate GLP-1 secretion, we investigated postprandial gallbladder emptying and GLP-1 responses in women with GDM. Methods: Women with and without GDM underwent two 240-min mixed meal tests; one during third trimester of pregnancy and one 3–6 months postpartum. We evaluated ultrasonography-assessed gallbladder emptying, plasma concentrations of glucometabolic hormones including GLP-1, paracetamol absorption (proxy for gastric emptying) and circulating factors known to affect gallbladder dynamics. Results: Fifteen women with GDM and 15 pregnant women with normal glucose tolerance (NGT) (baseline median age 31 (interquartile range 29;33) versus 32 (28;33) years, body mass index (BMI) 27.2 (24.7;30.7) versus 28.4 (26.2;31.0) kg/m2, HbA1c 30 (29;32) versus 30 (28;31) mmol/mol) were included. No differences in postprandial gallbladder emptying or GLP-1 responses were observed between women with and without GDM, neither during pregnancy nor postpartum. Pregnancy increased fasting gallbladder volumes by 69 (30;122)% and 103 (59;156)% and postprandial gallbladder emptying by 77 (28;236)% and 99 (37;190)% compared with postpartum in women with and without GDM, respectively. Postprandial GLP-1 responses were reduced by 60 (3;82)% and 81 (11;90)% during pregnancy compared with postpartum in women with and without GDM, respectively. Conclusion: Pregnancy-induced changes in gallbladder motility seem to play no or a limited role in previously reported GDM-associated reduced postprandial GLP-1 responses as gallbladder emptying was greater and postprandial GLP-1 response was lower in pregnancy than postpartum regardless of GDM status.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Gether, Ida M.","Andersen, Emilie S.","Foghsgaard, Signe","Ellegaard, Anne-Marie","Kelstrup, Louise","Sonne, David P.","Brønden, Andreas","Gillum, Matthew P.","Holst, Jens Juul","Hartmann, Bolette","Rehfeld, Jens F.","Vilsbøll, Tina","Knop, Filip K."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-790274"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cholecystokinin","Gestational diabetes mellitus","Glucagon Like Peptide 1","Glucose dependent insulinotropic polypeptide","Pregnancy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"increased gallbladder emptying and reduced glp 000000000001 response in pregnancy with and without gestational diabetes mellitus","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-790274","identifier":[{"id":"85209136433","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39543983","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-4fb5dd46-f227-44d0-b5f4-2fe134c9f56e"],"keyword":["cholecystokinin","gallbladder function","gestational diabetes mellitus","glucagon-like peptide 1","glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide","pregnancy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-52BF051883CC96B788348AAFE59A9CF3"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Pharmacology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Ida M.","key":"getherpau","last":"Gether","name":"Gether, Ida M.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Emilie S.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Emilie S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Signe","key":"foghsgaardpau","last":"Foghsgaard","name":"Foghsgaard, Signe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne-Marie","key":"ellegaardpau","last":"Ellegaard","name":"Ellegaard, Anne-Marie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise","key":"kelstruppau","last":"Kelstrup","name":"Kelstrup, Louise","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","first":"David P.","key":"sonnepau","last":"Sonne","locid":"7a31fbc9-91a2-4c55-b1b1-52dcc62f3158","name":"Sonne, David P.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","first":"Andreas","key":"brøndenpau","last":"Brønden","locid":"9bf1001e-ab98-4968-b9cb-154594128ce5","name":"Brønden, Andreas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Matthew P.","key":"gillumpau","last":"Gillum","locid":"65c5e8eb-5634-45db-952e-d28bf525bd32","name":"Gillum, Matthew P.","orcid":"0000-0003-4893-012X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jens J.","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","name_org":"Holst, Jens J.","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Bolette","key":"hartmannpau","last":"Hartmann","locid":"eb04fc6b-068a-4d5b-a106-1b7be3f7e12b","name":"Hartmann, Bolette","orcid":"0000-0001-8509-2036","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens F.","key":"rehfeldpau","last":"Rehfeld","name":"Rehfeld, Jens F.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Tina","key":"vilsbøllpau","last":"Vilsbøll","name":"Vilsbøll, Tina","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Filip K.","key":"knoppau","last":"Knop","locid":"ce6eaad9-59f8-4ecf-8a1e-388a74734f6a","name":"Knop, Filip K.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39543983"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/dom.16064","issn":["14628902","14631326"],"issn_org":["14628902"],"issue":"2","journal":"Diabetes, Obesity and Metabolism","pages":"697-709","status":"p","title":"Diabetes, Obesity and Metabolism","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85209136433"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4fb5dd46-f227-44d0-b5f4-2fe134c9f56e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Increased gallbladder emptying and reduced GLP-1 response in pregnancy with and without gestational diabetes mellitus","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-790274","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Osteogenesis imperfecta (OI) is a rare hereditary disease mainly resulting in reduced or altered collagen type I. Collagen type I is a major constituent of the respiratory system, and normal collagen type I is vital for pulmonary tissue function. RESEARCH QUESTION: Do patients with OI have increased admission rates resulting from pulmonary diseases compared with the general population? STUDY DESIGN AND METHODS: This was a register-based nationwide cohort study including all patients with OI in Denmark and a reference population. From January 1, 1995, through December 31, 2018, we evaluated the rates of admissions resulting from asthma, COPD, and pneumonia as well as the use of bronchodilator drugs and antibiotics comparing individuals with OI with the reference population. RESULTS: We included 862 individuals with OI and 4,283 people from the reference population covering 15,952 and 79,471 person-years of observation, respectively, in the two cohorts. The admissions rate (incidence rate [IR]) was highest in female patients with OI aged 65 years or older, with 56.3 admissions per 1,000 person-years and 29.4 admissions per 1,000 person-years in the reference population (amounting to an admissions incident rate ratio [IRR] of 1.91 [95% CI, 1.38-2.70]). The highest admission rate in male patients with OI was found among participants aged 0 to 18 years, with an IR of 30.4 per 1,000 person-years compared with an IR of 7.7 per 1,000 person-years in the reference population (IRR, 4.92 [95% CI, 3.79-6.38]). We found a higher proportion of long-acting and short-acting bronchodilator drug users in the OI cohort, but no increased use of antibiotics. INTERPRETATION: Overall, the admission rates for respiratory diseases were low in the OI cohort, but a higher relative risk of hospitalizations resulting from respiratory disease compared with the general population. Timely diagnosis and treatment of respiratory complications in individuals with OI is warranted.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Andersen, Jane Dahl","Lyster, Marie Louise","Holst, Mette Kathrine","Henriksen, Daniel Pilsgaard","Christensen, Anders","Laursen, Christian B","Forlino, Antonella","Folkestad, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-812733"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Folkestad, Lars"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Pavia"],"keyword":["Asthma","COPD","Collagen Type I","Epidemiology","Osteogenesis imperfecta","Pneumonia","Rare diseases","Register based"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"risk of pulmonary diseases in osteogenesis imperfecta in denmark a register based cohort study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.chest.2024.09.004","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-812733","identifier":[{"id":"39299390","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85216223331","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-c2ef2979-a9e7-4a19-b6b5-6b5443cd99b7"],"keyword":["COPD","asthma","collagen type I","epidemiology","osteogenesis imperfecta","pneumonia","rare diseases","register based"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-09CDECBF686F068765E109C34A31C82A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.chest.2024.09.004","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/286835118/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l