{"abstract":"Background: Emergence agitation and delirium in children remain a common clinical challenge in the post-anesthetic care unit. Preoperative oral melatonin has been suggested as an effective preventive drug with a favorable safety profile. The oral bioavailability of melatonin, however, is low. Therefore, the MELA-PAED trial aims to investigate the efficacy and safety of intraoperative intravenous melatonin for the prevention of emergence agitation in pediatric surgical patients. Methods: MELA-PAED is a randomized, double-blind, parallel two-arm, multi-center, superiority trial comparing intravenous melatonin with placebo. Four hundred participants aged 1–6 years will be randomized 1:1 to either the intervention or placebo. The intervention consists of intravenous melatonin 0.15 mg/kg administered approximately 30 min before the end of surgery. Participants will be monitored in the post-anesthetic care unit (PACU), and the Post Hospitalization Behavior Questionnaire for Ambulatory Surgery (PHBQ-AS) will be performed on days 1, 7, and 14 after the intervention. Serious Adverse Events (SAE) will be assessed up to 30 days after the intervention. Results: The primary outcome is the incidence of emergence agitation, assessed dichotomously as any Watcha score >2 during the participant's stay in the post-anesthetic care unit. Secondary outcomes are opioid consumption in the post-anesthetic care unit and adverse events. Exploratory outcomes include SAEs, postoperative pain, postoperative nausea and vomiting, and time to awakening, to first oral intake, and to discharge readiness. Conclusion: The MELA-PAED trial investigates the efficacy of intravenous intraoperative melatonin for the prevention of emergence agitation in pediatric surgical patients. Results may provide further knowledge concerning the use of melatonin in pediatric perioperative care.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Garioud, Anne Louise de Barros","Andersen, Lars Peter Kloster","Jensen, Aksel Karl Georg","Do, Hien Quoc","Jakobsen, Janus Christian","Holst, Lars Broksø","Rasmussen, Lars Simon","Afshari, Arash"],"cuid":["S02-088.89-725183"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Garioud, Anne Louise de Barros"],"keyword":["Anesthesia Recovery Period","Anesthetics","Anesthetics Inhalation adverse effects","Child","Children","Double Blind Method","Emergence Delirium prevention control","Emergence agitation","Emergence delirium","Humans","Melatonin","Melatonin therapeutic use","Multicenter Studies as Topic","Postoperative Period","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","Sevoflurane"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Danish Ministry of Defence Personnel Agency"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intravenous melatonin for prevention of postoperative agitation and emergence delirium in children mela paed a protocol and statistical analysis plan for a randomized clinical trial","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.14342","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-088.89-725183","identifier":[{"id":"37904610","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85175450356","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-5d1682c6-3d43-4229-a61d-ebde64d1610f","sdu-5da9e6d3-6f7b-4872-8cf9-b7e9c3e5afe7"],"keyword":["Anesthesia Recovery Period","Anesthetics","Anesthetics, Inhalation/adverse effects","Child","Double-Blind Method","Emergence Delirium/prevention & control","Humans","Melatonin/therapeutic use","Multicenter Studies as Topic","Postoperative Period","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","children","emergence agitation","emergence delirium","melatonin","sevoflurane"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3DB4AAD042317841C4F0161FEFB9BAC8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/257112986/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.14342","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/379867565/Acta_Anaesthesiol_Scand_2023_Garioud_Intravenous_MELAtonin_for_prevention_of_Postoperative_Agitation_and_Emergence.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Anaesthesiology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Køge"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2"