:"Damm, Peter","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jens J.","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","name_org":"Holst, Jens J.","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Filip K.","key":"knoppau","last":"Knop","locid":"ce6eaad9-59f8-4ecf-8a1e-388a74734f6a","name":"Knop, Filip K.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Tina","key":"vilsbøllpau","last":"Vilsbøll","locid":"76773372-af8c-45a0-9447-a509cbf6d466","name":"Vilsbøll, Tina","orcid":"0000-0002-0456-6787","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37846555"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/dom.15306","issn":["14628902","14631326"],"issn_org":["14628902"],"issue":"1","journal":"Diabetes, Obesity and Metabolism","pages":"201-214","status":"p","title":"Diabetes, Obesity and Metabolism","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85174239831"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0de20349-9817-4e24-a8b7-ba60590a291c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Liraglutide treatment for the prevention of glucose tolerance deterioration in women with prior gestational diabetes mellitus : A 52-week randomized controlled clinical trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-719274","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Implementation of therapeutic in vivo gene editing using CRISPR/Cas relies on potent delivery of gene editing tools. Administration of ribonucleoprotein (RNP) complexes consisting of Cas protein and single guide RNA (sgRNA) offers short-lived editing activity and safety advantages over conventional viral and non-viral gene and RNA delivery approaches. By engineering lentivirus-derived nanoparticles (LVNPs) to facilitate RNP delivery, we demonstrate effective administration of SpCas9 as well as SpCas9-derived base and prime editors (BE/PE) leading to gene editing in recipient cells. Unique Gag/GagPol protein fusion strategies facilitate RNP packaging in LVNPs, and refinement of LVNP stoichiometry supports optimized LVNP yield and incorporation of therapeutic payload. We demonstrate near instantaneous target DNA cleavage and complete RNP turnover within 4 days. As a result, LVNPs provide high on-target DNA cleavage and lower levels of off-target cleavage activity compared to standard RNP nucleofection in cultured cells. LVNPs accommodate BE/sgRNA and PE/epegRNA RNPs leading to base editing with reduced bystander editing and prime editing without detectable indel formation. Notably, in the mouse eye, we provide the first proof-of-concept for LVNP-directed in vivo gene disruption. Our findings establish LVNPs as promising vehicles for delivery of RNPs facilitating donor-free base and prime editing without formation of double-stranded DNA breaks.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Haldrup, Jakob","Andersen, Sofie","Labial, Alexander Rafael LaVilla","Wolff, Jonas Holst","Frandsen, Frederik Plum","Skov, Thomas Wisbech","Rovsing, Anne Bruun","Nielsen, Ian Helstrup","Jakobsen, Thomas Stax","Askou, Anne Louise","Thomsen, Martin K.","Corydon, Thomas J","Thomsen, Emil Aagaard","Mikkelsen, Jacob Giehm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-688310"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Mikkelsen, Jacob Giehm"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"engineered lentivirus derived nanoparticles lvnps for delivery of crispr cas ribonucleoprotein complexes supporting base editing prime editing and in vivo gene modification","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkad676","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-688310","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10570023","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85174939933","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37678882","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-db8eff41-ba9b-461e-a8d7-5dba04b84076"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-583C9FF4D423232503C26F280991EC56"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkad676","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Forskning og uddannelse, Skou-bygningen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"haldrupjakobpau","last":"Haldrup","locid":"38ce8dc0-5ce7-4717-be51-9eec11e6629f","name":"Haldrup, Jakob","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sofie","key":"andersensofiepau","last":"Andersen","locid":"fc30266f-8faa-48a5-8d20-d9f6c4c2668b","name":"Andersen, Sofie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander Rafael LaVilla","key":"labialalexanderrafaellavillapau","last":"Labial"