21"],"issn_org":["03906078"],"issue":"S1","journal":"Haematologica","pages":"13","paperid":"BA6","publisher":"Ferrata Storti Foundation","status":"p","title":"Haematologica","volume":"103"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2e93ef3e-a0c1-42fd-91fc-9ee0616eb58b"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Minimal Residual Disease (MRD) follow up of MM patients obtaining stringent complete remission (sCR) in the NMSG/EMN02 clinical trial – defining sCR numbers and prediction of disease progression by multiparametric flow cytometry (MFC).","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-063556","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: Type 2 diabetes increases the risk of nonalcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD), which is a potentially reversible condition but is also associated with progressive fibrosis and cirrhosis. Women with prior gestational diabetes mellitus (pGDM) have a higher risk for NAFLD. RESEARCH DESIGN AND METHODS: One hundred women without diabetes who had pGDM (median [interquartile range]: age 38.6 [6.4] years; BMI 31.0 [6.2] kg/m(2)) and 11 healthy control subjects without NAFLD (age 37.9 [7.8] years; BMI 28.1 [0.8] kg/m(2)) underwent a 75-g oral glucose tolerance test (OGTT), DXA whole-body scan, and ultrasonic evaluation of hepatic steatosis. RESULTS: Twenty-four (24%) women with pGDM had NAFLD on the basis of the ultrasound scan. None had cirrhosis. Women with NAFLD had a higher BMI (P = 0.0002) and waist circumference (P = 0.0003), increased insulin resistance (P = 0.0004), and delayed suppression of glucagon after the OGTT (P < 0.0001), but NAFLD was not associated with the degree of glucose intolerance (P = 0.2196). Visceral fat mass differed among the three groups, with the NAFLD group having the highest amount of fat and the control subjects the lowest (P = 0.0003). By logistic regression analysis, insulin resistance (P = 0.0057) and waist circumference (P = 0.0109) were independently associated with NAFLD. CONCLUSIONS: NAFLD was prevalent in this cohort of relatively young and nonseverely obese women with pGDM who are considered healthy apart from their increased risk for diabetes. Insulin resistance and a larger waist circumference were independently associated with the presence of NAFLD, whereas glucose intolerance was not.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Foghsgaard, Signe","Andreasen, Camilla","Vedtofte, Louise","Andersen, Emilie S.","Bahne, Emilie","Strandberg, Charlotte","Buhl, Thora","Holst, Jens Juul","Svare, Jens","Clausen, Tine Dalsgaard","Mathiesen, Elisabeth R.","Damm, Peter","Gluud, Lise Lotte","Knop, Filip K.","Vilsbøll, Tina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-402317"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nonalcoholic fatty liver disease is prevalent in women with prior gestational diabetes mellitus and independently associated with insulin resistance and waist circumference","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-402317","identifier":[{"id":"85008235593","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27810989","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-0eedd881-3133-4871-a1e2-9500505b38e8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B00CB8440BA3FAF6BA2E4A94A442BA73"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, NNF Center for Basic Metabolic Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Signe","key":"foghsgaardpau","last":"Foghsgaard","name":"Foghsgaard, Signe","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Camilla","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","name":"Andreasen, Camilla","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Louise","key":"vedtoftepau","last":"Vedtofte","name":"Vedtofte, Louise","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Emilie S.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Emilie S.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Emilie","key":"bahnepau","last":"Bahne","name":"Bahne, Emilie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte","key":"strandbergpau","last":"Strandberg","name":"Strandberg, Charlotte","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thora","key":"buhlpau","last":"Buhl","name":"Buhl, Thora","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jens J","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","name_org":"Holst, Jens J","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jens A","key":"svarepau","last":"Svare","locid":"4b9de77f-8ddc-4c1e-82ad-3d3f4a0be427","name":"Svare, Jens","name_org":"Svare, Jens A","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tine D","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","locid":"047e6356-0a01-48a6-9a2e-fa550c06183e","name":"Clausen, Tine Dalsgaard","name_org":"Clausen, Tine D","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Elisabeth R","key":"mathiesenpau","last":"Mathiesen","locid":"3acd58f4-6d64-4a89-a406-d2f43b310500","name":"Mathiesen, Elisabeth R.","name_org":"Mathiesen, Elisabeth R","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Peter","key":"dammpau","last":"Damm","locid":"884d03d5-5981-4d33-80c6-adb21f836deb","name":"Damm, Peter","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lise L","key":"gluudpau","last":"Gluud","locid":"5f316a6f-fef0-44ac-ad8d-522731684721","name":"Gluud, Lise Lotte","name_org":"Gluud, Lise L","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Filip K","key":"knoppau","last":"Knop","locid":"ce6eaad9-59f8-4ecf-8a1e-388a74734f6a","name":"Knop, Filip K.","name_org":"Knop, Filip K","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tina Vilsbøll","key":"lauritsenpau","last":"Lauritsen","locid":"76773372-af8c-45a0-9447-a509cbf6d466","name":"Vilsbøll, Tina","name_org":"Lauritsen, Tina Vilsbøll","orcid":"0000-0002-0456-6787","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27810989"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2337/dc16-1017","issn":["01495992"],"issue":"1","journal":"Diabetes Care","pages":"109-116","status":"p","title":"Diabetes Care","volume":"40"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85008235593"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0eedd881-3133-4871-a1e2-9500505b38e8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Nonalcoholic Fatty Liver Disease Is Prevalent in Women With Prior Gestational Diabetes Mellitus and Independently Associated With Insulin Resistance and Waist Circumference","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-402317","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"AIMS/HYPOTHESIS: We investigated whether a reduced incretin effect, as observed in patients with type 2 diabetes, can be detected in high-risk individuals, such as women with prior gestational diabetes mellitus (pGDM). METHODS: In this cross-sectional study, 102 women without diabetes with pGDM and 15 control participants without pGDM and with normal glucose tolerance (NGT) underwent a 4 h 75 g OGTT and an isoglycaemic i.v. glucose infusion (IIGI). Women with pGDM were classified as having NGT or prediabetes (impaired fasting glucose and/or impaired glucose tolerance). Insulin sensitivity was assessed using the Matsuda index and HOMA2-IR and the incretin effect was calculated from insulin responses during the study (100% × [AUCinsulin,OGTT - AUCinsulin,IIGI]/AUCinsulin,OGTT). RESULTS: Sixty-three of the 102 women with pGDM (62%) had prediabetes (median [interquartile range]: age, 38.3 [6.5] years; BMI, 32.1 [5.8] kg/m(2)) and 39 women (38%) had NGT (age, 39.5 [5.6] years; BMI, 31.0 [6.7] kg/m(2)). Control participants (n = 15) were not significantly different from the pGDM group with regards to age (39.2 [7.4] years) and BMI (28.8 [9.2] kg/m(2)). Compared with women with NGT and control participants, women with prediabetes had lower insulin sensitivity, as measured by the Matsuda index (3.0 [2.4] vs 5.0 [2.6] vs 1.5 [1.8], respectively; p < 0.001). The incretin effect was 55.3% [27.8], 73.8% [19.0] and 76.7% [24.6] in women with prediabetes, women with normal glucose tolerance and control participants, respectively (p < 0.01). CONCLUSION/INTERPRETATION: Prediabetes was highly prevalent in women with pGDM, and alterations in the incretin effect were detected in this group before the development of type 2 diabetes. TRIAL REGISTRATION: clinicaltrialsregister.eu 2012-001371-37-DK.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Foghsgaard, Signe","Vedtofte, Louise","Andreasen, Camilla","Andersen, Emilie S","Bahne, Emilie","Bagger, Jonatan I","Svare, Jens","Holst, Jens Juul","Clausen, Tine Dalsgaard","Mathiesen, Elisabeth R.","Damm, Peter","Knop, Filip K.","Vilsbøll, Tina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-475747"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"women with prior gestational diabetes mellitus and prediabetes are characterised by a decreased incretin effect","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-475747","identifier":[{"id":"85016573408","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28364253","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-899f18b0-56ec-40d1-ae37-54080eabde02"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7595E81F9774EF67A21ABA99835B7182"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Signe","key":"foghsgaardpau","last":"Foghsgaard","name":"Foghsgaard, Signe","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Louise","key":"vedtoftepau","last":"Vedtofte","name":"Vedtofte, Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Camilla","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","name":"Andreasen, Camilla","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Emilie S","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Emilie S","rank":4,"role