y of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-899f18b0-56ec-40d1-ae37-54080eabde02"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Women with prior gestational diabetes mellitus and prediabetes are characterised by a decreased incretin effect","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-475747","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Preterm infants often tolerate full enteral nutrition few weeks after birth but it is not known how this is related to gut maturation. Using pigs as models, we hypothesized that intestinal structure and digestive function are similar in preterm and term individuals at 3-4 weeks after birth and that early enteral nutrition promotes maturation. METHODS: Preterm or term cesarean-delivered pigs were fed total parenteral nutrition (TPN), or partial enteral nutrition (ENT, 16-64 mL/kg/d of bovine colostrum) for 5 d, followed by full enteral milk feeding until d 26. The intestine was collected for histological and biochemical analyses at d 0, 5 and 26 (n = 8-12 in each of ten treatment groups). RESULTS: Intestinal weight (relative to body weight) was reduced in preterm pigs at 0-5 d but ENT feeding stimulated the mucosal volume and peptidase activities. Relative to term pigs, mucosal volume remained reduced in preterm pigs until 26 d although plasma glucagon-like peptide 2 (GLP-2) and glucose-dependent insulin-trophic peptide (GIP) levels were increased. Preterm pigs also showed reduced hexose absorptive capacity and brush-border enzyme (sucrase, maltase) activities at 26 d, relative to term pigs. CONCLUSION: Intestinal structure shows a remarkable growth adaptation in the first week after preterm birth, especially with enteral nutrition, while some digestive functions remain immature until at least 3-4 weeks. It is important to identify feeding regimens that stimulate intestinal maturation in the postnatal period of preterm infants because some intestinal functions may show long-term developmental delay.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Hansen, Carl Frederik","Thymann, Thomas","Andersen, Anders Daniel","Holst, Jens Juul","Hartmann, Bolette","Hilsted, Linda","Langhorn, Louise","Jelsing, Jacob","Sangild, Per Torp"],"cuid":["S02-098.99-041782"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Animals","Animals Newborn","Digestion","Enzymes","Gestational Age","Glucagon Like Peptide 2","Hexoses","Intestinal Absorption","Intestinal Mucosa","Journal Article","Prematurity","Swine"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-GUB"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-GUB","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rapid gut growth but persistent delay in digestive function in the postnatal period of preterm pigs","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84983788979","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.99-041782","identifier":[{"id":"26822913","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84983788979","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4836131","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-3fb9355b-b69b-441e-9b42-5ac7d52d3533","sdu-6478ddaa-b090-4243-8bca-1807e9c245a0"],"keyword":["Animals","Animals, Newborn","Digestion","Enzymes","Gestational Age","Glucagon-Like Peptide 2","Gut development","Hexoses","Intestinal Absorption","Intestinal Mucosa","Journal Article","Prematurity","Swine","alpha-Fetoproteins"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1C5934BD5261F9EB598EF8BE83962586"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences, Comparative Paediatrics and Nutrition","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Comparative Pediatrics and Nutrition"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"gubra","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-GUB","l3nl":"Gubra","l3nn":"Gubra","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Gubra","namevar":["Gubra"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-GUB","used":1},{"affno":4,"key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Biomedical Laboratory"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Carl Frederik","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Carl Frederik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"thymannpau","last":"Thymann","locid":"f137235e-3711-4a1d-b108-bc6ab7602f8e","name":"Thymann, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0001-7480-6064","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Daniel","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"db12a91e-c481-422d-aadd-14c85c8e46a7","name":"Andersen, Anders Daniel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bolette","key":"hartmannpau","last":"Hartmann","locid":"eb04fc6b-068a-4d5b-a106-1b7be3f7e12b","name":"Hartmann, Bolette","orcid":"0000-0001-8509-2036","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Linda","key":"hilstedpau","last":"Hilsted","locid":"b51cc15d-e5af-476e-b0bd-12b56481f0bd","name":"Hilsted, Linda","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise","key":"langhornpau","last":"Langhorn","locid":"afa67a98-9fbd-43ae-b201-b6fa69a5be37","name":"Langhorn, Louise","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jacob","key":"jelsingpau","last":"Jelsing","name":"Jelsing, Jacob","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Per T","key":"sangildpau","last":"Sangild","locid":"d0225a7f-ad88-418d-8660-bff37f7358d9","name":"Sangild, Per Torp","name_org":"Sangild, Per T","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26822913"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1152/ajpgi.00221.2015","issn":["01931857","15221547"],"issn_org":["01931857"],"issue":"8","journal":"American Journal of Physiology: Gastrointestinal and Liver Physiology","publisher":"American Physiological Society","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Physiology: Gastrointestinal and Liver Physiology","volume":"310"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84983788979"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Gubra","Hospitals","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3fb9355b-b69b-441e-9b42-5ac7d52d3533","sdu-6478ddaa-b090-4243-8bca-1807e9c245a0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Rapid gut growth but persistent delay in digestive function in the postnatal period of preterm pigs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.99-041782","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"AIMS/HYPOTHESIS: The influence of glucagon on glycaemic control in type 1 diabetes is debated. We investigated the relationship between postprandial glucagon levels and HbA1c during a period up to 60 months after diagnosis of childhood type 1 diabetes. METHODS: The Danish remission phase cohort comprised 129 children (66 boys) with type 1 diabetes whose mean (SD) age at onset was 10.0 (3.9) years. Liquid mixed-meal tests were performed prospectively at 1, 3, 6 and 12 months and a subset of 40 patients completed follow-up at 60 months. Postprandial (90 min) plasma levels of glucagon, glucose (PG), C-peptide, total glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP-1), glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide (GIP) and HbA1c were analysed. Multivariate regression (repeated measurements with all five visits included) was applied and results expressed as relative change (95% CI). RESULTS: Postprandial glucagon levels increased 160% from 1 to 60 months after diagnosis (p < 0.0001). A doubling in postprandial PG corresponded to a 21% increase in postprandial glucagon levels (p = 0.0079), whereas a doubling in total GLP-1 levels corresponded to a 33% increase in glucagon levels (p < 0.0001). Postprandial glucagon associated negatively with postprandial C-peptide (p = 0.017). A doubling in postprandial glucagon corresponded to a 3% relative increase in HbA1c levels (p = 0.0045). CONCLUSIONS/INTERPRETATION: Postprandial glucagon levels were associated with deterioration of glycaemic control and declining beta cell function in the first 5 years after diagnosis of type 1 diabetes. The positive association of glucagon with total GLP-1 and PG suggests that physiological regulation of alpha cell secretion in type 1 diabetes is seriously disturbed.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Fredheim, Siri","Andersen, Marie-Louise M","Pörksen, Sven","Nielsen, Lotte B","Pipper, Christian Bressen","Hansen, Lars","Holst, Jens Juul","Thomsen, Jane","Johannesen, Jesper","Mortensen, Henrik B","Svensson, Jannet"],"cuid":["S02-098.57-047488"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Alpha cell regulation","Children","Glucagon","Glucagon Like Peptide 1","Glucose dependent insulinotropic polypeptide","Glycaemic control","Type 1 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the influence of glucagon on postprandial hyperglycaemia in children 000000000005 years after onset of type 000000000001 diabetes","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84925465190","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.57-047488","identifier":[{"id":"25541633","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84925465190","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f77802b6-6c96-407b-ba0f-89d54f0b57fa","sdu-d25ebfc5-3b52-4f9f-9660-94f4d6d2fb57"],"keyword":["Alpha cell regulation","Children","Glucagon","Glucagon-like peptide-1","Glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide","Glycaemic control","Type 1 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C4DC9390424E982C094E74E0CCEA9CBB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Paediatrics (Kolding)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Siri","key":"fredheimpau","last":"Fredheim","locid":"834b9d9f-0f77-498e-bd73-0210623e3ddf","name":"Fredheim, Siri","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marie-Louise M","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Marie-Louise M","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sven","key":"pörksenpau","last":"Pörksen","name":"Pörksen, Sven","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lotte B","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lotte B","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"pipperpau","last":"Pipper","locid":"c002fade-f477-46eb-aa1f-34702fdd3746","name":"Pipper, Christian Bressen","name_org":"Pipper, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-0261-616X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Lars","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jane","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"7be933b9-8685-4e2f-90b2-5aebacecfb0f","name":"Thomsen, Jane","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"johannesenpau","last":"Johannesen","locid":"f8330122-dfc2-46b6-823b-95cdf4efab03","name":"Johannesen, Jesper","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik B","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"f1a10f64-1be6-42df-b4ee-7df370fcc9d0","name":"Mortensen, Henrik B","orcid":"0000-0001-9231-8363","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jannet","key":"svenssonpau","last":"Svensson","locid":"404145c9-3f7a-4360-81ae-2ee5a9ca2173","name":"Svensson, Jannet","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25541633"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00125-014-3486-3","issn":["0012186X","14320428"],"issn_org":["0012186X"],"issue":"4","journal":"Diabetologia","pages":"828-834","publisher":"Springer Science+Business Media","status":"p","title":"Diabetologia","volume":"58"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84925465190"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f77802b6-6c96-407b-ba0f-89d54f0b57fa","sdu-d25ebfc5-3b52-4f9f-9660-94f4d6d2fb57"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The influence of glucagon on postprandial hyperglycaemia in children 5 years after onset of type 1 diabetes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.57-047488","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"ABSTRACT: BACKGROUND: Research shows that obesity prevention has to start early. Targeting interventions towards subgroups of individuals who are predisposed, but yet normal weight, may prove more effective in preventing overweight than interventions towards unselected normal weight subsets. Finally, interventions focused on other factors than diet and activity are lacking. The objectives were to perform a randomized, controlled intervention aiming at preventing overweight in children aged 2-6 years, who are yet normal weight, but have high predisposition for future overweight, and to intervene not only by improving diet and physical activity, but also reduce stress and improve sleep quality and quantity. METHODS: Based on information from the Danish national birth registry and administrative birth forms, children were selected based on having either high birth weight, a mother who was overweight prior to pregnancy, or a familial low socioeconomic status. Selected children (n = 5,902) were randomized into three groups; an intervention group, a shadow control group followed in registers exclusively, and a control group examined at the beginning and at the end of the intervention. Approximately 21% agreed to participate. Children who presented as overweight prior to the intervention were excluded from this study (n = 92). In the intervention group, 271 children were included, and in the control group 272 were included. Information obtained from the shadow control group is on-going, but it is estimated that 394 children will be included. The intervention took place over on average 11/2 year, between 2009 and 2011, and consisted of optional individual guidance in optimizing diet and physical activity habits, reducing chronic stress and stressful events and improving sleep quality and quantity. The intervention also included participation in cooking classes and play arrangements. Information on dietary intake, meal habits, physical activity, sleep habits, and overall stress level was obtained by 4-7 day questionnaire dairies and objective measurements. DISCUSSION: If the Healthy Start project is effective in preventing excessive weight gain, it will provide valuable information on new determinants of obesity that should be considered in future interventions, and on new strategies to prevent development of overweight and obesity at an early age. Trial Registration Number: NCT01583335.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Olsen, Nanna J","Buch-Andersen, Tine","Händel, Mina N","Ostergaard, Louise M","Pedersen, Jeanet","Seeger, Charlotte","Stougaard, Maria","Trærup, Maria","Livemore, Kate","Mortensen, Erik Lykke","Holst, Claus","Heitmann, Berit L"],"cuid":["S02-096.40-044312"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the healthy start project a randomized controlled intervention to prevent overweight among normal weight preschool children at high risk of future overweight","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2458-12-590","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-096.40-044312","identifier":[{"id":"22852799","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84864409788","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3490801","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-8e5d7a62-8e2f-46d5-a03e-474d89ad0bac","sdu-ff718da3-7365-4a29-ac6c-78a22520e6f5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2DFB2EBE909B22A5F0BD439365AC692B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2458-12-590","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","c